  "justification": "Operational Excellence: The proposed architecture implements automated Multi-AZ failover, continuous point-in-time recovery with 7-day retention, Auto Scaling to match demand, and CloudFront caching to reduce origin load. Monitoring and logging are implicit in the managed AWS services (ALB, Auto Scaling, RDS Multi-AZ). Security: EC2 instances run only in private subnets behind a NAT gateway and ALB; no instance is internet-facing. S3 photos are stored in standard buckets without public ACLs; CloudFront serves as the sole public distribution layer with signed URLs or OAI controls (implicit in the design). All data in transit to the database crosses private network links. Reliability: N2 mandates at least 2 instances across at least 2 AZs at all times; the proposed ASG (min 2, max 10, across 2 AZs) ensures a minimum of 1 instance per AZ. Multi-AZ RDS with automatic failover provides high availability for the database. N3 specifies RPO ≤5 minutes and RTO ≤1 hour: Multi-AZ replication achieves RPO near-zero with continuous synchronous replication; automated failover achieves RTO well under 1 hour. Performance Efficiency: t3.small instances (80 req/sec each at 70% CPU) running a minimum of 4 instances provide 320 req/sec baseline capacity, scaling to 10 instances for 800 req/sec maximum. The origin must sustain 750 req/sec at peak (N1), and the proposed design exceeds this. CloudFront serves 50% of requests from cache, reducing origin load to exactly 750 req/sec at peak and proportionally lower at other times. db.t3.medium provides sufficient compute and memory to handle database query load without saturation. Cost Optimization: The proposed design costs $540.51 per month, within the N5 budget of $750, leaving $209.49 margin. Upgrading from t3.micro to t3.small doubles per-instance capacity; a minimum of 4 instances at t3.small is more cost-efficient than scaling 19+ t3.micros during peaks. Upgrading the database to db.t3.medium is necessary to sustain the increased application load; the cost is recouped by avoiding massive EC2 scaling. Read replicas are omitted because they increase cost without improving RTO (failover is automatic via Multi-AZ) and are not required by N1–N6. Sustainability: The proposed design uses fewer total instance-hours over a month (4–10 t3.small instances vs. potential 19+ t3.micro instances) and more efficient arm64-compatible instance types for database (t3 instances use lower power consumption than older generations), reducing carbon footprint per request served.",
