h 5-day PITR satisfy RPO; minimum 2 instances across 2 AZs ensure web tier survives single-AZ failure; ASG self-healing replaces failed instances automatically; CloudFront edge caching provides resilience against origin outages; the proposed architecture adds capacity headroom (50 req/s) for surge tolerance.\n\n*Performance Efficiency:* t3.small instances deliver 2× throughput of t3.micro at 2× hourly cost, meeting peak demand with headroom; ASG scales to only 2 instances during average-load periods (150 req/s origin demand requires 2 instances at 80 req/s each), reducing waste relative to running maximum capacity; CloudFront caches 50% of requests, cutting origin load from 1,500 to 750 req/s at peak; compute utilization remains optimal at 70% target CPU during peak events.\n\n*Cost Optimization:* The proposed architecture costs only $360.14/month versus $358.76 for the original, a 0.4% increase despite 10× traffic growth on CloudFront. This is achieved by retaining small database and compute footprints during off-peak periods; t3.small provides sufficient capacity at manageable cost; monthly total is 52% below the $750 budget, leaving substantial headroom for growth; reserved instance or savings plan purchases could reduce costs further. The minimal cost increase demonstrates efficient right-sizing.",
